<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionIRI> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA/3.0> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-10-5" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Fatima Danash and Marc-Andree Wolf"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "LCA (Life Cycle Assessment) module of an EU DPP (Digital Product Passport) core ontology proposal of the CIRPASS-2 European project.\n\nSCOPE\nThis module covers environmental-performance metadata that a DPP needs to carry and is based on the ILCD+EPD v1.3 data format (https://indatawg.github.io/ILCD-EPD-Data-Format/). \nIt supports both (a) general LCA studies of any product, expressed via eudpp:LCAStudy, and (b) Environmental Product Declarations (EPDs) conforming to EN 15804+A2 with EF 3.1 characterisation, expressed via eudpp:EPDStudy (a subclass of LCAStudy). \n\nDEPENDENCIES\nThis module imports the ACTOR module of the CIRPASS-2 EU DPP Core Ontology (https://w3id.org/eudpp/ACTOR) for its eudpp:Actor and eudpp:Facility classes. It also references, but does not import, the Ontology of Units of Measure (OM-2; http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/) for units. Cross-module object properties whose domain is in this module and whose range is in another EUDPP module (Actor, Facility, Product, DPP) are NOT defined here; per the EU DPP Core Ontology design principles, they are defined in the CONNECTOR module. The full list of Connector entries that this module expects is given in the per-class comments below."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026-10-16" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "This ontology is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. In case of dispute over Apache 2.0 applicability, or in case considering the ontology as a document, this ontology document is to be considered licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "LCA module of the CIRPASS-2 EU DPP Core Ontology"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "eudpp" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> "https://w3id.org/eudpp#" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The LCA module of the EU DPP core ontology, version 3.0"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "EU DPP LCA"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://indatawg.github.io/ILCD-EPD-Data-Format/> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://standards.cen.eu/dyn/www/f?p=204:110:0::::FSP_PROJECT:65243> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#priorVersion> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA/2.0> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/LCA> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "3.0"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
