<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EPDDocument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Source> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EPDDocument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Source representing the published PDF or HTML EPD document itself (as distinct from the ILCD+EPD machine-readable EPDStudy)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EPDDocument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "EPD Document"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EPDDocument> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broadMatch> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EPDDocument> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "ILCD+EPD extension"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#EPDStudy
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EPDStudy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EPDStudy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAStudy> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EPDStudy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An LCA study that conforms to EN 15804+A2 with EF 3.1 characterisation, i.e. an Environmental Product Declaration. Inherits all study-level metadata from eudpp:LCAStudy (compliance declarations, manufacturer records, reviews, LCA results, etc.) and adds EPD-specific properties: ILCD+EPD format version (eudpp:epdFormatVersion), registration number, expiry date, reference to the published EPD document (eudpp:EPDDocument via referenceToOriginalEPD), reference to the applicable Product Category Rules (eudpp:PCR via referenceToPCR). EN 15804+A2 module values per LCAResult are used to populate per-life-cycle-module values. Replaces v1.9.4's mixed structure and v1.9.5's eudpp:EPDDataSet."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EPDStudy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "EPD Study"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EPDStudy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "EPD-Studie"@de .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EPDStudy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://indatawg.github.io/ILCD-EPD-Data-Format/doc/> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EPDStudy> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "ILCD+EPD extension"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnergyConsumptionResult
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnergyConsumptionResult> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnergyConsumptionResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#InventoryIndicatorResult> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnergyConsumptionResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An LCA inventory indicator result quantifying the consumption of primary energy resources — renewable and non-renewable — in a product system. \nCommonly associated with the EN 15804+A2 primary energy indicators (e.g. PERE, PERM, PERT, PENRE, PENRM, PENRT), though no formal quantifiesIndicator restriction is imposed, as energy consumption may span multiple indicators depending on the study scope."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnergyConsumptionResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Energy Consumption Result"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnergyConsumptionResult> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCA ontology"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnvironmentalFootprintScore
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnvironmentalFootprintScore> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnvironmentalFootprintScore> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAIndicator> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnvironmentalFootprintScore> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An aggregated single-score indicator computed as the normalised and weighted sum of a set of impact-category results. \nHolds one named individual eudpp:ind_EF_singleScore representing the EU Environmental Footprint single score (PEF score). The applied normalisation factors and weighting set are not modelled here as properties; they are determined by the active EF / PEF methodology version, which is resolvable via the study's eudpp:hasComplianceDeclaration link to a eudpp:ComplianceSystem source. \nResults computed for an EnvironmentalFootprintScore individual are eudpp:LCIAResult instances."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnvironmentalFootprintScore> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Environmental Footprint Score"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnvironmentalFootprintScore> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCA ontology"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnvironmentalFootprintScoreResult
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnvironmentalFootprintScoreResult> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnvironmentalFootprintScoreResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAResult> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnvironmentalFootprintScoreResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid26 .
_:genid26 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onClass> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnvironmentalFootprintScore> .
_:genid26 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#qualifiedCardinality> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger> .
_:genid26 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#quantifiesIndicator> .
_:genid26 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnvironmentalFootprintScoreResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A normalized and weighted aggregate LCA result expressing the overall environmental performance of a product system as a single dimensionless score, computed by applying the Product Environmental Footprint (PEF) method (Recommendation (EU) 2021/2279). \nAggregates the characterised results of all 16 EF 3.1 impact categories through normalization and weighting factors.\nInstances of this class quantify the EF single score indicator (ind_EF_singleScore, an EnvironmentalFootprintScore individual) via quantifiesIndicator."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnvironmentalFootprintScoreResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Environmental Footprint Score Result"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EnvironmentalFootprintScoreResult> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCA ontology: third sibling subclass of eudpp:LCAResult alongside eudpp:LCIAResult and eudpp:InventoryIndicatorResult, introduced to represent the aggregated EF single score result."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#ImpactModel
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ImpactModel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ImpactModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The characterisation model underlying an LCIA method (e.g. IPCC AR6 2021 for GWP). It carries a model name (eudpp:modelName), optional version (eudpp:modelVersion), and optional bibliographic source (eudpp:referenceToModelSource)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ImpactModel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Impact Model"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ImpactModel> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "ILCD+EPD extension: corresponds to the element impactModel of an LCIA Method Data Set."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#ImpactModel> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCAnet: relates to the element CharacterizationModel (https://w3id.org/lcanet/ia#CharacterizationModel) of the IA module."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#InventoryIndicatorResult
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#InventoryIndicatorResult> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#InventoryIndicatorResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAResult> .
