<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodology> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodology> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A named, versioned LCA methodology (a coherent set of LCA methods sharing principles and a set of characterisation factors), to which one or more Method instances belong. \nEach individual SHOULD carry a skos:altLabel giving a short code (e.g. \"EF 3.1\") and eudpp:methodologyVersion giving the version identifier."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodology> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LCA Methodology"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodology> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCA ontology"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAMethodology> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCAnet: relates to the element Methodology (https://w3id.org/lcanet/ia#Methodology) of the IA module."@en .
