# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCIAImpactIndicator
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCIAImpactIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCIAImpactIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCAIndicator> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCIAImpactIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A characterised impact indicator outside the EN 15804+A2 selection — direct subclass of eudpp:LCAIndicator, sibling of eudpp:EN15804Indicator. Holds the 16 official EF 3.1 / PEF impact category indicators as named individuals (Andreasi Bassi et al., JRC, 2023). \nThese are the impact indicators used by general LCA studies (eudpp:LCAStudy) following the EU Environmental Footprint method, distinct from the EN 15804+A2 set used by EPDStudy. \nThe two sets overlap conceptually — both have e.g. a \"Climate change\" indicator with kg CO2-eq — but differ operationally: EN 15804+A2 splits Climate change into four sub-indicators (total, fossil, biogenic, luluc) and selects 6 \"with caveats\" indicators with EN-specific reporting rules; EF 3.1 keeps Climate change as one indicator and presents 16 categories at one aggregation level."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCIAImpactIndicator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LCIA Impact Indicator"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCIAImpactIndicator> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCA ontology"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCIAImpactIndicator> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCAnet: relates to the element ImpactCategoryIndicator (https://w3id.org/lcanet/ia#ImpactCategoryIndicator) of the IA module."@en .
