<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LifeCycleModule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A modelled life-cycle module per EN 15804+A2 (product stage A1-A3, construction A4-A5, use stage B1-B7, end-of-life C1-C4, benefits/loads D). Enumeration of 18 named individuals. \nNote that moduleA1A3 (aggregated product stage) is an alternative reporting form of A1+A2+A3; an EPD that reports A1-A3 should not additionally report A1, A2, A3 separately for the same indicator/scenario."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LifeCycleModule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Life Cycle Module"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#LifeCycleModule> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "ILCD+EPD extension"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#MaterialFootprint
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#MaterialFootprint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#MaterialFootprint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#InventoryIndicatorResult> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#MaterialFootprint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An InventoryIndicatorResult that \"refers to the total amount of raw materials extracted to meet final consumption demands\" (ESPR Art. 2(26)).\n\nModelled as an inventory-level result rather than a characterised LCIA result, as it aggregates raw material extraction flows without applying characterisation factors.\nNo single EN 15804+A2 inventory indicator individual is pinned via quantifiesIndicator; the link is left to individual instances, as material footprint spans multiple EN 15804+A2 resource use inventory indicators (PERE, PENRE, SM, RSF, NRSF, etc.)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#MaterialFootprint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Material Footprint"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#MaterialFootprint> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "ESPR Art 2 (26) https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#MaterialFootprint> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "LCAnet: relates to the element MaterialFootprint (https://w3id.org/lcanet/ia#MaterialFootprint) of the IA module."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#PCR
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#PCR> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#PCR> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Source> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#PCR> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Source that is a Product Category Rules document (EN 15804+A2 Table 2 Line 1). Used in EN 15804+A2 EPDStudy via eudpp:referenceToPCR."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#PCR> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Product Category Rules (PCR)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#PCR> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broadMatch> <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#PCR> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#sourceVocabulary> "ILCD base"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#PEFCR
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#PEFCR> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#PEFCR> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Source> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#PEFCR> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Source that is a Product Environmental Footprint Category Rules document, the European Commission Environmental Footprint methodology's product-category-specific rules. Parallel role to PCR but for PEF studies (rather than EN 15804+A2 EPD studies). Used by an LCAStudy via eudpp:referenceToPEFCR. NEW in v1.9.7."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#PEFCR> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Product Environmental Footprint Category Rules (PEFCR)"@en .
